{"book":5,"chapter":17,"context":{"chapter":17,"title":"A King Under the Law","summary":"After laws on sacrifices, witnesses and hard court cases, Moses anticipates a king. He must be God's choice, must not pile up horses, wives or gold, and must read God's law daily.","background":"Israel did ask for a king 'like all the nations' (1 Samuel 8:5). Solomon later did all three things this chapter forbids, gathering horses from Egypt, many foreign wives and great wealth (1 Kings 10–11). The king's 'copy of this law' (v. 18) was rendered 'second law' in the Greek translation, which gave the book its English name.","customs":[{"term":"Two or three witnesses","verses":"17:6","note":"No one could be executed on one witness's word. The rule is restated in 19:15 and used in Matthew 18:16."},{"term":"Horses from Egypt","verses":"17:16","note":"Horses meant chariots and military power, and Egypt was a known source. Gathering them meant trusting force and drawing Israel back toward Egypt."}],"watchFor":["Three limits on the king (vv. 16–17).","The king is first of all a reader of the law (vv. 18–19).","'That his heart be not lifted up above his brethren' (v. 20)."],"connections":["1 Samuel 8:5","1 Kings 10:26-29","1 Kings 11:1-3","Matthew 18:16"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["לֹא","lo'-","H3808","HTn","not"],["תִזְבַּח","tizbach","H2076","HVqi2ms","you will sacrifice"],["לַיהוָה","layahweh","H3068","HR/Npt","to Yahweh"],["אֱלֹהֶיךָ","'eloheikha","H430","HNcmpc/Sp2ms","God your"],["שׁוֹר","shor","H7794","HNcmsa","an ox"],["וָשֶׂה","vaseh","H7716","HC/Ncbsa","and a sheep"],["אֲשֶׁר","'asher","H834","HTr","which"],["יִהְיֶה","yihyeh","H1961","HVqi3ms","it will be"],["בוֹ","vo","H9033","HRd/Sp3ms","in <the> it"],["מוּם","mum","H3971","HNcmsa","a blemish"],["כֹּל","kol","H3605","HNcmsc","any"],["דָּבָר","davar","H1697","HNcmsa","thing"],["רָע","ra'","H7451","HAamsa","bad"],["כִּי","ki","H3588","HTc","for"],["תוֹעֲבַת","to'avat","H8441","HNcfsc","[is] [the] abomination of"],["יְהוָה","yahweh